NAME
     dig - ask the name server

SYNOPSIS
     dig [@SERVER] NAME [TYPE] [+short]
     dig -x ADDRESS
     host NAME

DESCRIPTION
     dig sends a DNS query and prints the answer section in full. TYPE
     is A, AAAA, CNAME, MX, NS, PTR, SOA or TXT.

OPTIONS
     @SERVER   ask this server rather than the configured one
     +short    the answer alone
     -x ADDR   a reverse lookup

SEE ALSO
     nslookup(1), ping(1), /etc/resolv.conf
